## 27. Preregistration — Gospel of Judas, Egyptian dyadic fractions, and numerical-generative pattern audit

**Evidence status:** `[preregistered][targeted-current-Core-scan-pending]`; no targeted systematic scan of the current Core implementation under the frozen numerical-family and transform rules below had begun when this section was defined. This section is a scope and anti-cherry-picking lock, not a positive numerical result.

### 27.1 Owner clue and governing interpretation rule

The project owner introduced a deliberately broad out-of-the-box clue set: the Gospel of Judas numerical/cosmological hierarchy, the Egyptian dyadic fraction sequence often associated with the Eye of Horus/Rhind tradition, the golden ratio, Fibonacci recurrence, prime structure, Riemann-zeta zeros, and any mathematically meaningful relation that might also occur in current Lineum implementation or reproducible Lineum results.

The binding interpretation rule is:

```text
numerical or structural resemblance = possible clue only
possible clue + frozen null rejection = hypothesis candidate
hypothesis candidate + preregistered discriminating Lineum test = research evidence within that tested domain
resemblance alone = never proof
```

The scientific target is therefore not to collect attractive equalities. It is to ask whether the **same generator, recurrence, operator, symmetry, factorization, scaling law, or dimensionless causal structure** occurs independently in Lineum and survives controls that would make a coincidence easy.

### 27.2 Chronology and prior-exposure disclosure

Global numerical blindness cannot honestly be claimed. Earlier Lineum work exposed many parameters, counts, ratios, and outputs before this checkpoint. The current protection is narrower and explicit: the systematic scan of current Core against the registered families and transform budget below begins only after this scope lock.

A machine-readable companion scope lock was published first as

